# Frontend rules

Source: `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` §6; DESIGN_SYSTEM (from PR-M2); GENERATIVE_UI (from PR-M4).

- Boundaries (ARCH-R035): `app/` imports only `features/` and `lib/`; only `lib/api/` performs fetch or EventSource; only `packages/viz` imports `echarts`; only `agui/` imports `@ag-ui/*`; nothing imports `app/`. (Checked: ESLint boundaries in `make frontend-lint`.)
- Server Components render the shell only. All data is fetched client-side through `lib/api` over the same-origin `/api` rewrite and parsed with the generated zod schema. Unparsed data is never rendered. (Checked: AT-M0-T04-06.)
- Query keys start with `[principalId, datasetId, …]`; sign-out or a persona switch clears the cache.
- Client state has exactly the owners in ARCHITECTURE §6.5 (React context + `useReducer`; no global state library). Scope and grants are never held as authority on the client.
- The route map of ARCHITECTURE §6.2 is fixed; overlays use search parameters (§6.8). Deep links carry identifiers only.
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; no API or model string as HTML, URL, `href`, `src` or style. (Checked: ESLint `react/no-danger`.)
- Never import or hand-write a contract type; use `packages/contracts-ts` (GENERATED). (Checked: `make contracts-check`.)
- Every screen state is accessible: keyboard reachable, announced, no colour-only signals. axe-core serious or critical findings fail E2E.
- The synthetic banner and as-of date are visible on every screen.
- TypeScript strict; ESLint zero warnings; Prettier formatted.
